<title>EGYPT: Egyptian trade deficit falls in Nov 1996.</title>
<headline>Egyptian trade deficit falls in Nov 1996.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's trade deficit fell to 2.504 billion pounds ($740 million) in November 1996, from 2.738 billion in October and 2.599 billion in November 1995.</p>
<p>The Central Agency for Public Mobilisation and Statistics, the government statistics office, gave these trade figures on Monday (all figures in millions of pounds):</p>
<p>			     Nov 1996     Oct 1996     Nov 1995</p>
<p> Imports		   3,445.5	 3,706.8	3,478.8</p>
<p> Exports		     941.5	   968.5	  879.8</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>     Oil and products    455.5	   450.2	  376.6</p>
<p>     Non-oil		 478.2	   513.7	  478.9</p>
<p>     Re-exports		7.9	     4.6	   24.3</p>
<p> TRADE DEFICIT	   2,504.0	 2,738.4	2,599.0</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>				Jan-Nov 1996	 Jan-Nov 1995</p>
<p> Imports			39,553.1		35,927.8</p>
<p> Exports			11,312.6		11,201.9</p>
<p>of which:</p>
<p>     Oil and products	5,174.8		 4,011.7</p>
<p>     Non-oil		   5,902.7		 6,969.4</p>
<p>     Re-exports		  235.1		   220.8</p>
<p> TRADE DEFICIT		28,240.4		24,725.9</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
